%-------------------------
% Resume in Latex
% Author : Jake Gutierrez
% Jinja-ified for render.py (JSON-Resume dict -> LaTeX) by the ATS pipeline.
%-------------------------
%%
%% Rendered by render.py through a Jinja2 environment configured with
%% LaTeX-safe delimiters so ordinary TeX braces never collide with Jinja.
%% The delimiters are: VAR (variable interpolation, already LaTeX-escaped in
%% Python), BLOCK (control flow: if / for / endif / endfor) and a hash-brace
%% Jinja comment form. Do NOT write those delimiter tokens literally in this
%% file outside of an actual tag -- Jinja parses them wherever they appear,
%% even inside a LaTeX comment.
%%
%% Every interpolated value is escaped in render.py (& % $ # _ { } ~ ^ \) and
%% passed in as either an escaped string or a null. The contact line is built
%% in render.py as ready-made \href markup (raw URL target, escaped display).
%% Optional fields are wrapped in BLOCK-if guards so a missing value emits
%% *nothing* -- no placeholder text, no dangling "$|$" separators, no empty
%% itemize environments.

\documentclass[letterpaper,11pt]{article}

\usepackage{latexsym}
\usepackage[empty]{fullpage}
\usepackage{titlesec}
\usepackage{marvosym}
\usepackage[usenames,dvipsnames]{color}
\usepackage{verbatim}
\usepackage{enumitem}
\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}
\usepackage{fancyhdr}
\usepackage[english]{babel}
\usepackage{tabularx}


%----------FONT OPTIONS----------
% sans-serif
% \usepackage[sfdefault]{FiraSans}
